!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Human lung tissues were used for total RNA extraction with RNeasy Plus Mini Kit (Qiagen) according to the manufacturer’s protocol. RNA purity was assessed using a Nanodrop ND-2000 (Thermo Scientific), and each RNA sample had an A260:A280 ratio above 1.8 and an A260:A230 ratio above 2.0. RNA integrity was evaluated using the Agilent 2200 TapeStation (Agilent Technologies), and each sample had the RNA Integrity Number (RIN) above 7.0. The ribosomal RNAs (rRNAs) were removed using Ribo-Zero rRNA Removal Kits (Illumina).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA libraries were then constructed by NEBNext Ultra RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (New England Biolabs) and evaluated using the Agilent 2200 TapeStation and Qubit® 2.0 (Life Technologies). Sequencing was performed by RiboBio Co., Ltd. on an Illumina HiSeq 3000 machine with paired-end 150-bp reads.
!Sample_data_processing = The adaptors and low quality bases assessed using FASTQC 0.11.3 were trimmed by Trimmomatic 0.39 using the following options: TRAILING:20, MINLEN:235 and CROP:235
!Sample_data_processing = Trimmed reads were then aligned to the ensembl 79 (GRCh38.p2) reference genome using STAR 2.4.2a
!Sample_data_processing = FeatureCounts 1.6.2 was subsequently employed to convert aligned short reads into read counts for each sample
!Sample_data_processing = The data were then analyzed using R 3.4.4 and DEseq2 1.18.1. Differentially expressed genes of each disease group were identified using Wald statistics test, with fold-change > 2 and Benjamini–Hochberg (BH)-adjusted P < 0.1 as compared to NC group
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: ensembl 79 (GRCh38.p2)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab-delimited text files include raw count values
